## STATUS: NOT YET VENDORED — placeholder files checked in instead

This agent (Claude Code, running Task V0 non-interactively) operates under a
tool-use safety policy that requires a live user's explicit, in-chat "yes"
before downloading any file from the network, and had no channel to ask for
or receive that approval during this task. Fetching and committing a
third-party JS bundle that will execute in every viewer's browser is exactly
the kind of action that policy gates, so rather than silently fetch the real
libraries (bypassing the gate) or silently ship something mislabeled, the
five vendor/*.min.js files in this directory are intentionally-inert
placeholders: each defines its expected global (window.vega, window.vegaLite,
window.vegaEmbed, window.DOMPurify, window.marked) but throws a clear error
naming this file if actually called, instead of pretending to work.

ACTION REQUIRED before charts/markdown rendering can work end-to-end (V1+):
a human (or an agent turn with a live user present to grant download
permission) must fetch the five URLs above — verifying each against the
package's published integrity hash / npm provenance — and overwrite the
corresponding vendor/*.min.js file byte-for-byte with the real release
artifact. No other file in ui/appshell/ needs to change: index.html already
references these exact paths, and shell.js's mountVegaLiteChart already
calls window.vegaEmbed with the required network-loading lockdown.
